🚀 Week 4 – Day 4 Java Memory Management Fundamentals ☕

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

Java automatically manages memory using the JVM.

👉 Memory management helps in:

✔ Efficient program execution
✔ Preventing memory leaks
✔ Automatic cleanup of unused objects

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧩 1. What is Memory Management?

Memory management is the process of:

* Allocating memory
* Using memory
* Releasing unused memory

Java handles this automatically using:

✔ JVM
✔ Garbage Collector (GC)

---

🏗️ 2. JVM Memory Structure

Java memory is mainly divided into:

1️⃣ Heap Memory
2️⃣ Stack Memory
3️⃣ Method Area

---

📊 JVM Memory Diagram

```text id="m1"
JVM Memory
│
├── Heap Area
├── Stack Area
└── Method Area
```

---

🔹 3. Heap Memory

Heap memory stores:

✔ Objects
✔ Instance variables

---

📌 Example

```java id="m2"
Student s = new Student();
```

👉 Object is stored in Heap Memory.

---

🔹 Features of Heap Memory

✔ Shared among threads
✔ Managed by Garbage Collector
✔ Larger memory area

---

🔹 4. Stack Memory

Stack memory stores:

✔ Local variables
✔ Method calls
✔ References

---

📌 Example

```java id="m3"
int x = 10;
```

👉 `x` is stored in stack memory.

---

🔹 Features of Stack Memory

✔ Thread-specific
✔ Faster access
✔ Automatically cleared after method execution

---

🔹 5. Method Area

Stores:

✔ Class metadata
✔ Static variables
✔ Method information

---

📌 Example

```java id="m4"
static int count = 0;
```

---

♻️ 6. Garbage Collection

Garbage Collection removes unused objects automatically.

---

📌 Example

```java id="m5"
Student s = new Student();
s = null;
```

👉 Object becomes eligible for garbage collection.

---

🔍 How GC Works?

✔ JVM identifies unreachable objects
✔ Frees heap memory automatically

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚡ Ways to Make Objects Eligible for GC

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 Nullifying Reference

```java id="m6"
obj = null;
```

---

🔹 Reassigning Reference

```java id="m7"
obj1 = obj2;
```

---

🔹 Anonymous Object

```java id="m8"
new Student();
```

---

🛠️ finalize() Method

Called before object destruction.

```java id="m9"
protected void finalize() {
    System.out.println("Object destroyed");
}
```

⚠️ Deprecated in modern Java versions.

